s","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"fd2f19ad8da0f8d63c75dcbeca2fdf5a337d4c6869dc6929b00158e0ff1ecf0e"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":22980,"output_tokens":1259,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"a42306d7b3739e9133fb70d7471f29c9c69c9bcdb85caf3ff96c250c4b43a4d0"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":29812,"output_tokens":1288,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"1ea5b5ccf6c6179191c7c29453d5777f27f9f34ed5998cfb3810c25d865cd41a"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":210070,"output_tokens":5354,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm WHICH directory `identity._git_email` interrogates on the failing doctor-repair path (does `run_repair`/`doctor_cli` route `config.repo_root()` to the monkeypatched `tracker`, or elsewhere?), and reconcile that with the fact the 5 failing tests ALREADY set repo-local `user.email` via `_git_backed`; state the fix in terms of the directory the repair path actually queries, not merely 'the subprocesses the test spawns.'","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["All 5 failing tests set repo-local identity: test_repair_force_writes... at tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py:365-373 runs `('config','user.email','t@example.invalid')`; the shared helper `_git_backed` at tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py:445-453 does the same and is called by test_run_repair (l.479), test_json_output (l.516), test_repair_refuses (l.605), test_unrepairable (l.653).","`_repair_pause.owned_repair_pause` (src/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py:114-117) calls `identity._git_email(root)`; `_git_email` (src/rebar/_commands/identity.py:86-108) runs `git config user.email` with `cwd = str(repo_root or config.repo_root())` — a repo-local value in that cwd would be found, so a locally-established identity is NOT missing per se.","The scrubbed GIT_CONFIG_* injection was command-scope and thus cwd-independent — it would satisfy `git config user.email` from ANY directory, which suggests the failing path queries identity from a directory OTHER than the tracker where the tests set it (a repo-root routing mismatch), not from an absence of identity."],"finding":"The plan's root-cause-to-fix mechanism ('tests relied on injected identity; establish an explicit local identity') is contradicted by the failing tests, which already establish a repo-local `user.email` via `_git_backed` / inline `git config user.email`; the fix as described may re-do what the tests already do and not resolve the failure.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe392cff3ffe470ae","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'Give the affected tests an explicit, known-good git identity for the subprocesses they spawn'; Root cause section","norm_id":"na7244633dbfadea8","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds a shared helper that sets repo-local user.email exactly as `_git_backed` already does, reruns the 5 nodeids, and they still fail because the repair path's `config.repo_root()` resolves to a directory with no configured identity.","The AC 'a subprocess spawned by the shared identity helper sees a configured user.email' passes in isolation, yet the doctor repair path still returns None because it queries a different repo root."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Before prescribing the helper, trace `doctor.run_repair`/`doctor_cli` -> `_repair_pause.owned_repair_pause` -> `identity._git_email(root)` to determine the effective `repo_root`. If it is not the tmp `tracker`, the helper must establish identity in that directory (or the plan must route `repo_root` to the tracker). Add the traced repo-root 