rom) so the proving pytest invocation is unambiguous.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The 20 git-identity nodeids fixed by 985f still pass, proving the scrub was not weakened.'","The 5 test_doctor.py nodeids are enumerated verbatim in Observation; the 20 are not listed anywhere in the plan."],"finding":"AC2 references '20 git-identity nodeids fixed by 985f' but does not enumerate them, unlike the 5 doctor nodeids which are listed explicitly. The executor cannot run the exact set to prove the scrub was not weakened without going to fetch the 985f ticket's list.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd9af17f558fb8ed2","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, bullet 2","norm_id":"nb42bab4844ceb2b3","priority":0.165,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must verify AC2 but has to reconstruct which 20 nodeids from the 985f ticket."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"List the 20 nodeids inline, or add a pointer like 'the nodeid list recorded on 985f-0ec5-a61c-46ee' so AC2's pytest command is reproducible.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State whether the shared identity helper sets identity per-subprocess-invocation (scoped, auto-retired) or mutates os.environ (session-wide), and confirm it does NOT re-leak ambient identity that would re-break the 20 scrub-isolated tests.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Prefer a single shared helper alongside scrub_ambient_git_config ... so the two concerns — remove ambient identity, establish a deliberate one — sit together'","The scrub is explicitly session-wide and mutates the real process environment (conftest.py:168 in pytest_configure); a helper following the same pattern would leak identity back into os.environ for the rest of the session."],"finding":"The plan introduces a shared identity helper alongside scrub_ambient_git_config but never states HOW it establishes the identity for subprocesses — per-invocation subprocess env vs. mutating the real os.environ. If it mutates process environment the way the scrub does, it re-introduces a session-wide mutable-state leak (the very concern the scrub addresses) with no defined create/retire lifecycle, undermining the isolation the scrub bought for the other 20 tests.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4312f7a367e74d5d","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: 'a single shared helper alongside scrub_ambient_git_config in tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py'","norm_id":"n6af85d26fd0bce48","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the helper writes GIT_CONFIG_* / user.email back into os.environ, every subsequent subprocess in the session inherits a deliberate identity — silently re-establishing ambient identity and re-breaking the 20 tests the scrub isolated.","If instead it sets per-invocation subprocess env, the identity is scoped and retired automatically — but the plan does not say which, leaving ownership/retirement undefined."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify the helper returns/populates a subprocess-local env (e.g. an env dict passed to subprocess.run) rather than mutating os.environ, so the deliberate identity is scoped to the spawned process and retired when it exits — keeping the session-wide scrub intact.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"799606ca925d3872","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["56f70c11f774ea1c",5458],"description_boxes":["90a512a5b8a10706",0],"file_impact":["79a1116e74d68f67",3],"ticket_id":["91506ed752a27caf",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":330498,"cache_write_tokens":131879,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":3754.9,"input_